# Encrypted broker credential material (Fernet-encrypted JSON per elements_v2.md §1.2)
*credentials*.json
*creds*.json

# Non-Plane artifacts only (logs/ per directory_structure.md) — never commit these anyway
logs/*
!logs/.gitkeep

# pg_dump staging (Backblaze pipeline) — binary/compressed backup artifacts only.
# databases/schema/ (extracted DDL — the source-of-truth schema artifacts) IS tracked;
# directory_structure.md explicitly scopes "auxiliary DB files" into this directory,
# and a blanket databases/* rule silently defeated that. Never the PG cluster itself
# (that lives at the OS-default location per elements_v2.md, outside ~/nix entirely).
databases/*.dump
databases/*.sql.gz
databases/*.tar
databases/backups/

# Node-identity / runtime state (state/ — hardware UUID, credential JSON). Not for a
# public repo: the hardware UUID is machine-fingerprinting info, not a secret exactly,
# but not something to publish either. credentials.json is already covered above by
# *credentials*.json but state/ is excluded wholesale for defense in depth.
#
# BOTH SPELLINGS, AND THE SLASHLESS ONE IS LOAD-BEARING (ARC 022). `state/` matches a
# DIRECTORY only. In the primary tree state/ is a directory, so it is ignored — but
# `scripts/provision_worktree.sh` links it into every worktree as a SYMLINK, which the
# trailing-slash pattern does not match. ARC 022 measured `git check-ignore` exiting 1
# in a provisioned worktree: the symlink was untracked-but-not-ignored, and the
# mandatory `git add -A` before every gate measurement staged a symlink pointing at the
# 0600 directory holding the hardware UUID and credential JSON. The provisioning
# script's own docstring asserted these "cannot be committed"; that claim was false.
# This is the same defect as the .testmondata sidecars below — a bare pattern not
# covering every spelling of its subject — caught by ARC 016 in this same file.
state
state/

# Env / master-password material
*.env
.env
*master_password*
*master-password*

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
# `.venv` slashless for the same ARC 022 reason as `state` above: the provisioned
# worktree holds a SYMLINK, and `.venv/` matches directories only.
.venv
.venv/
venv/
# ARC CRUCIBLE-DEPSPLIT: the generator-only dev venv (calendar_gen.py's
# pandas_market_calendars tree). Same slashless/slash pairing as .venv above.
.venv-dev
.venv-dev/
# testmon's SQLite database and its WAL/shared-memory sidecars. The bare name alone
# did NOT cover the sidecars, and ARC 016 caught `.testmondata-shm` / `.testmondata-wal`
# being staged by a `git add -A`. Committing them would put a machine-local, constantly
# rewritten binary cache into history and make every commit conflict on it.
.testmondata
.testmondata-shm
.testmondata-wal

# macOS cruft (not part of the tracked tree)
.DS_Store
._*

# graphify working output (not part of this arc's scope)
graphify-out/

# Subagent-driven-development scratch workspace (ledgers, briefs, review packages)
.superpowers/

# Local Claude Code launcher (operator convenience, never published)
scripts/cl.sh

# Inbound CODE drafts delivered into downloads/ by claude.ai. The arc briefs
# (downloads/arc_*.md) ARE tracked — they are the design authority for an arc and
# history should hold them. The .py drafts are NOT: every one of them has since been
# landed under scripts/ and evolved well past the delivered version (ARC 016 measured
# broker_seam 626 -> 790 lines, simulate 258 -> 525, test_broker_order 489 -> 1270).
# Committing them would put a second, stale copy of live code in the tree — a
# derive-never-restate violation (CLAUDE.md directive 3) that the gate would then lint
# as if it were real, and that a future reader could mistake for the implementation.
# The landed file under scripts/ is the single source of truth.
downloads/*.py

# ARC 025: `verify.py --optimize` writes its DERIVED plan to
# `checks/<registry>.json.proposed` on every run, as a proposal that `--commit`
# then installs. It is a transient derivation artifact, never an input to
# anything — the plan of record is `checks/registry.json`, and the proposal is
# reproducible from the checks folder at any time.
#
# It is ignored for the reason D2.24 exists: this project MANDATES `git add -A`
# before every gate measurement, so an unignored generated file reaches the
# index on the first measurement any agent takes after running `--optimize`.
# That is the same shape as the `state/` symlink defect — a generated path
# entering history because nobody wrote the rule — and it was found here by the
# staging step doing exactly what it was designed to catch. Committing it would
# also put a SECOND copy of the execution plan in the tree, which is the
# derive-never-restate violation directly above, one directory over.
checks/*.proposed
